PART 18: COMMON MISTAKES
================================================================================

MISTAKE 1:

FORGETTING TO START LOADING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Request begins

but:

isLoading remains false


Result:

No loading feedback.


================================================================================
MISTAKE 2:

STOPPING LOADING ONLY ON SUCCESS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

try {

  ...

  setIsLoading(false)

} catch (error) {

  setError(
    error.message
  )
}


Problem:

Failure can leave:

isLoading = true


================================================================================
MISTAKE 3:

NO HTTP STATUS CHECK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const response =
  await fetch(url)


const data =
  await response.json()


Problem:

HTTP 500 may be treated like a normal response.


Use:

if (!response.ok) {

  throw new Error(...)
}


================================================================================
MISTAKE 4:

CONFUSING EMPTY WITH LOADING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

books = []


can mean:

• Request hasn't finished

or:

• Request successfully returned no records


That's why:

isLoading


is separate from:

books


================================================================================
MISTAKE 5:

SHOWING FULL-SCREEN LOADING DURING EVERY REFRESH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

If existing data is already available, replacing everything with:

Loading...


can cause unnecessary UI flicker.


Consider:

Existing Content
+
Refreshing...


================================================================================
QUICK REVISION TABLE
================================================================================

+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| CONCEPT                 | REMEMBER                                   |
+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| isLoading               | Is relevant request currently pending?     |
| setIsLoading(true)      | Start loading                              |
| setIsLoading(false)     | Finish loading                             |
| data                    | Successful backend result                  |
| error                   | Request failure                            |
| finally                 | Shared completion logic                    |
| Empty State             | Successful request with zero records       |
| AbortController         | Cancel obsolete request                    |
| role="status"           | Accessible loading feedback                |
| role="alert"            | Accessible error feedback                  |
| isRefreshing            | Background refresh state                   |
+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+


================================================================================
QUICK REVISION - FOUR UI STATES
================================================================================

1. LOADING

Request in progress


2. ERROR

Request failed


3. EMPTY

Request succeeded but returned no data


4. SUCCESS

Request succeeded and returned data


================================================================================
ONE-LINE MEMORY FORMULAS
================================================================================

START:

setIsLoading(true)


SUCCESS:

setData(result)


ERROR:

setError(message)


FINISH:

setIsLoading(false)


COMPLETE:

REQUEST
 ↓
LOADING
 ↓
SUCCESS / FAILURE
 ↓
FINAL UI


LOADING STATE:

isLoading === true

means:

REQUEST PENDING


EMPTY STATE:

isLoading === false

AND

data.length === 0

means:

REQUEST FINISHED
BUT NO DATA


================================================================================
MOST IMPORTANT RULE
================================================================================

LOADING IS NOT THE SAME AS EMPTY.

LOADING:

THE RESPONSE HAS NOT FINISHED YET.


EMPTY:

THE RESPONSE FINISHED SUCCESSFULLY,
BUT THERE ARE NO RECORDS.


A GOOD BACKEND-DRIVEN REACT UI SHOULD CLEARLY REPRESENT:

LOADING
+
ERROR
+
EMPTY
+
SUCCESS


